    "result_text": "The full suite passes \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (where YY is the last two digits of the registrationDate year, e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipNumber.java`** (new) \u2014 an OfficeFloor function that reads the owner via `@Val`, derives `YY` from `registrationDate.getYear() % 100` (zero-padded), and sets `membershipNumber` to `<customerCode>-M<YY>`.\n\n3. **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `assignMembershipNumber` step into the pipeline between `assignCustomerCode` and `countNamesakes` (so both the customer code and the defaulted registration date are already present), under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it into the GET response automatically.\n\n5. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `membership_number` column to the `owners` table so the field persists and reads back (tests use the `hsqldb` schema with `ddl-auto=none`).\n\nThe test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `coreMembershipNumberFormat` passes).",
